  "note": "\"The retiring members were returned unopposed.\" White is styled J.P. The Northern Whig (7 January 1932, p. 8) and the Banbridge Chronicle (9 January 1932, p. 1) also report \"no contest\" but name only seven, leaving out Dickson and Hanna. Polling day for the urban councils was Friday 15 January 1932. Joseph R. Cullen: no party label printed in 1932, and no report of this election states one. The label Nationalist shown before 7 Nov 2026 came from a later statement, not a report of this election: Portadown Times, 23 May 1952, p. 7 (filed source): J. R. Cullen \"the only Nationalist on the old Council\" (statement covers the 1949 council; applied to his 1926-1949 rows. His son Joseph Cullen (1952-) is not covered)."
